TITLE:: BroadcastStemTable
summary:: The stem assignment table behind Broadcast: index ↔ proxy, stable for the session
categories:: Live Coding>Synesthesia
related:: Classes/Broadcast, Guides/Synesthesia

DESCRIPTION::
Pure bookkeeping used by link::Classes/Broadcast::. Index 0 is always the main mix
(code::\main::). An index is given out once per proxy for the life of the table and
handed back only by link::#-release::, which Broadcast calls when the proxy's source
goes nil — so a proxy keeps its stem through code::.stop::/code::.play:: cycles and
source swaps, and the receiver can learn "stem 3 is the kick" once. A released index
is reused by the next new proxy. Unit-tested in code::TestBroadcast::.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: size
how many proxy stems beyond the main mix

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: assign
The proxy's index, assigning the lowest free one if it has none; code::nil:: when
the table is full.
argument:: proxy
argument:: key
the ProxySpace key, as published

METHOD:: release
Hand the proxy's index back; returns it, or nil.

METHOD:: indexOf
METHOD:: keyOf
The index / key held by a proxy, or nil.

METHOD:: keys
The table as published on code::/syn/stems::: an Array of keys by index, nil for a
free slot, code::\main:: at 0.

METHOD:: proxies
Every proxy currently holding an index.

METHOD:: count
How many proxies hold an index.

METHOD:: size
The number of proxy stems (not counting the main mix).

EXAMPLES::
code::
t = BroadcastStemTable(3);
t.assign(~k, \k);   // -> 1
t.assign(~a, \a);   // -> 2
t.assign(~k, \k);   // -> 1 (stable)
t.release(~k);      // -> 1
t.keys;             // -> [ main, nil, a, nil ]
::
